1
00:00:19,019 --> 00:00:20,368
We've just received a report

2
00:00:20,455 --> 00:00:21,978
the victim
has been identified

3
00:00:22,065 --> 00:00:24,807
'by the San Francisco locals
as Natalie Gibecki'

4
00:00:24,894 --> 00:00:26,461
although police are
keeping the nature

5
00:00:26,548 --> 00:00:30,378
of her death under wraps
for the moment they were..

6
00:00:30,465 --> 00:00:33,555
Her name's Natalie Gibecki.
27 years old.

7
00:00:33,642 --> 00:00:36,558
Works as a counselor in a youth
probation facility nearby.

8
00:00:36,645 --> 00:00:39,561
The mayor serves on the board,
so we got the call.

9
00:00:39,648 --> 00:00:41,432
Petechial hemorrhaging
in the eyes

10
00:00:41,519 --> 00:00:44,261
and the marks around the neck
indicate that she was strangled.

11
00:00:44,348 --> 00:00:47,308
- Mmm. Where's Lisbon?
- She's with S.F.P.D.

12
00:00:47,395 --> 00:00:48,874
They talked
to the victim's boss.

13
00:00:48,961 --> 00:00:50,920
She was headed
to a movie with friends.

14
00:00:51,007 --> 00:00:52,487
- Not likely.
- Come again?

15
00:00:52,574 --> 00:00:55,011
[Jane]
'Well, she's wearing
a black lace camisole.'

16
00:00:55,098 --> 00:00:58,667
She was planning on changing
her flats to heels.

17
00:00:58,754 --> 00:01:00,408
Her makeup is
freshly applied.

18
00:01:00,495 --> 00:01:01,713
She's wearing a very..

19
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:03,324
[sniffs]
Very flowery perfume..

20
00:01:03,411 --> 00:01:05,630
'J'adore, if I'm not mistaken.'

21
00:01:05,717 --> 00:01:08,068
She was going
to meet a lover.

22
00:01:08,155 --> 00:01:12,246
Married, I'd guess,
based on the deception.

23
00:01:12,333 --> 00:01:14,291
[cell phone ringing]
Excuse me.

24
00:01:14,378 --> 00:01:17,120
[clears throat]

25
00:01:17,207 --> 00:01:18,426
Hello?

26
00:01:18,513 --> 00:01:20,906
'Hello, Patrick.
It's Erica Flynn.'

27
00:01:20,993 --> 00:01:24,040
Erica Flynn.
Wow, this is a surprise.

28
00:01:24,127 --> 00:01:26,564
Pleasant, I hope.

29
00:01:26,651 --> 00:01:28,958
I bet you're wondering
why I'm calling.

30
00:01:29,045 --> 00:01:31,134
Yeah. Thought crossed my mind.

31
00:01:31,221 --> 00:01:33,397
What if I said
I wanted to hear you?

32
00:01:33,484 --> 00:01:34,877
'I'd say you were lying.'

33
00:01:34,964 --> 00:01:37,053
Not entirely.

34
00:01:37,140 --> 00:01:38,968
Natalie Gibecki..

35
00:01:39,055 --> 00:01:40,839
...I knew her personally.

36
00:01:40,926 --> 00:01:42,885
She was a client
of my matchmaking company.

37
00:01:42,972 --> 00:01:46,323
- I'm sorry for your loss.
- Thank you.

38
00:01:46,410 --> 00:01:49,587
We grew very close
during our sessions together

39
00:01:49,674 --> 00:01:51,676
but then you know
how that can happen.

40
00:01:51,763 --> 00:01:53,374
What do you want, Erica?

41
00:01:53,461 --> 00:01:54,897
Yes, I haven't said,
have I?

42
00:01:54,984 --> 00:01:56,638
'No.'

43
00:01:56,725 --> 00:01:59,162
I'm calling because I can
help you find her killer.

44
00:01:59,249 --> 00:02:00,816
Really? What's his name?

45
00:02:00,903 --> 00:02:03,384
'If you want the answer,
you know where I am.'

46
00:02:03,471 --> 00:02:05,168
It was nice hearing
your voice again.

47
00:02:05,255 --> 00:02:06,387
Yours, too.

48
00:02:12,262 --> 00:02:14,569
- Thank you, Dennis.
- Of course, Ms. Flynn.

49
00:02:14,656 --> 00:02:16,919
[Flynn]
'Helpful as always.'

50
00:02:17,006 --> 00:02:18,877
- Who was that?
- Uh..

51
00:02:18,964 --> 00:02:20,749
That was Erica Flynn.

52
00:02:20,836 --> 00:02:22,794
She wants to help out
with the investigation.

53
00:02:22,881 --> 00:02:25,884
We should fax over
the case file and get her a gun.

54
00:02:25,971 --> 00:02:28,060
Getting her a gun's
a bit much, but

55
00:02:28,148 --> 00:02:30,106
I think
the case file may help.

56
00:02:30,193 --> 00:02:31,281
I was kidding.

57
00:02:31,368 --> 00:02:32,630
[chuckles]
Yeah.

58
00:02:32,717 --> 00:02:34,415
You're kidding, right?

59
00:02:38,549 --> 00:02:39,855
Please tell me
you're kidding.

60
00:02:39,942 --> 00:02:42,336
[theme music]

61
00:03:00,005 --> 00:03:01,485
Hello, Patrick.

62
00:03:01,572 --> 00:03:04,619
Erica. You look good.

63
00:03:04,706 --> 00:03:06,316
Orange suits you.

64
00:03:06,403 --> 00:03:08,840
I suppose I have you
to thank for my wardrobe.

65
00:03:08,927 --> 00:03:10,451
I didn't kill your husband.

66
00:03:10,538 --> 00:03:13,367
Neither did I.
Manslaughter. Big difference.

67
00:03:13,454 --> 00:03:14,933
What is this about?

68
00:03:15,020 --> 00:03:16,718
I know
who killed Natalie Gibecki.

69
00:03:16,805 --> 00:03:18,589
How is that possible?

70
00:03:18,676 --> 00:03:21,201
We grew close
during our sessions together.

71
00:03:21,288 --> 00:03:24,029
Natalie told me things that
she didn't tell anyone else

72
00:03:24,116 --> 00:03:26,684
like the fact that she was
seeing someone in secret.

73
00:03:26,771 --> 00:03:29,948
Why'd she need a dating service
if she was seeing someone?

74
00:03:30,035 --> 00:03:31,733
She met him
during our sessions together.

75
00:03:31,820 --> 00:03:33,343
That must've been
some time ago.

76
00:03:33,430 --> 00:03:35,432
Ten months..

77
00:03:35,519 --> 00:03:38,174
...but Natalie was still
seeing him when she died.

78
00:03:38,261 --> 00:03:40,437
- I'm sure of it.
- How?

79
00:03:40,524 --> 00:03:42,874
I know true love
when I see it.

80
00:03:42,961 --> 00:03:44,528
Then why the secrecy?

81
00:03:44,615 --> 00:03:47,401
The man Natalie was
seeing was married.

82
00:03:47,488 --> 00:03:49,011
She kept the affair
from everyone.

83
00:03:49,098 --> 00:03:51,013
- Everyone except you.
- Yes.

84
00:03:55,452 --> 00:03:57,367
Why are you doing this?

85
00:03:57,454 --> 00:04:00,327
I cared deeply
about Natalie.

86
00:04:00,414 --> 00:04:03,895
Her death is a tragedy, and her
killer should be punished.

87
00:04:03,982 --> 00:04:06,768
That was a nice try.

88
00:04:06,855 --> 00:04:08,944
[whispering]
Alright. I want out of here.

89
00:04:09,031 --> 00:04:11,120
Temporarily, of course.

90
00:04:11,207 --> 00:04:14,166
You have no idea
what this is like, Patrick

91
00:04:14,254 --> 00:04:16,908
living in a cage..

92
00:04:16,995 --> 00:04:18,867
...knowing I'll be
here for years.

93
00:04:21,261 --> 00:04:24,481
The truth is, this may be
my last chance at freedom

94
00:04:24,568 --> 00:04:26,962
while I'm young enough
to enjoy it.

95
00:04:27,049 --> 00:04:31,532
I just want to go to the spa,
eat at my favorite restaurant

96
00:04:31,619 --> 00:04:33,011
a few harmless indulgences

97
00:04:33,098 --> 00:04:35,187
in return for helping you
catch a killer.

98
00:04:35,275 --> 00:04:37,755
What if you're lying?

99
00:04:37,842 --> 00:04:40,932
You once said you could
see right through me.

100
00:04:41,019 --> 00:04:44,022
"Transparent as glass,"
I believe, was how you put it

101
00:04:44,109 --> 00:04:45,981
so tell me,
am I lying now?

102
00:04:49,767 --> 00:04:52,857
[Kimball]
'Natalie Gibecki left
the youth facility at 8:14 p.m.'

103
00:04:52,944 --> 00:04:54,903
A commuter found her at 8:33

104
00:04:54,990 --> 00:04:57,384
giving us a 19-minute window
for the murder.

105
00:04:57,471 --> 00:04:59,081
What do we have for motive?

106
00:04:59,168 --> 00:05:01,605
There's nothing missing from
the body, so robbery seems out.

107
00:05:01,692 --> 00:05:03,433
No sign of sexual assault.

108
00:05:03,520 --> 00:05:06,741
She'd just returned from
a 5-day trip to Puerto Vallarta.

109
00:05:06,828 --> 00:05:08,612
Jane's theory
about a boyfriend?

110
00:05:08,699 --> 00:05:11,223
We looked into it. Friends say
Natalie wasn't seeing anyone.

111
00:05:11,311 --> 00:05:13,008
- Family?
- Only child.

112
00:05:13,095 --> 00:05:14,749
- Parents died years ago.
- Alright.

113
00:05:14,836 --> 00:05:17,012
Head to the youth facility,
talk to the counselors

114
00:05:17,099 --> 00:05:19,580
that were working on her shifts.

115
00:05:19,667 --> 00:05:21,625
Can I skip
this and work the phones?

116
00:05:21,712 --> 00:05:23,584
I have an appointment
in an hour.

117
00:05:23,671 --> 00:05:25,194
- Are you alright?
- Yeah, everything's fine.

118
00:05:25,281 --> 00:05:26,761
It's just something
I gotta do.

119
00:05:26,848 --> 00:05:28,893
- Sure. Van Pelt?
- Sure. On it.

120
00:05:33,942 --> 00:05:36,901
Hi. I'm Agent Van Pelt.
This is Agent Cho from CBI.

121
00:05:36,988 --> 00:05:39,208
We're here investigating
Natalie Gibecki's murder.

122
00:05:39,295 --> 00:05:41,993
I don't know how we'll tell
the boys. They loved Natalie.

123
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:44,126
You guys have
any idea who did this?

124
00:05:44,213 --> 00:05:45,823
We're in the
investigation's early stages.

125
00:05:45,910 --> 00:05:47,608
We believe
that Natalie may have been

126
00:05:47,695 --> 00:05:49,174
romantically involved
with someone.

127
00:05:49,261 --> 00:05:52,439
- You know anything about that?
- No.

128
00:05:52,526 --> 00:05:54,745
Yeah, no. I thought
she was single. Hey, Kevin!

129
00:05:54,832 --> 00:05:57,357
'Keep that up, you'll be doing
push-ups until you puke.'

130
00:05:57,444 --> 00:06:00,447
The relationship could have
been with a co-worker.

131
00:06:00,534 --> 00:06:02,492
- Don't look at me.
- You didn't like her?

132
00:06:02,579 --> 00:06:04,755
I didn't say that.
She just wasn't my type.

133
00:06:04,842 --> 00:06:07,410
Kevin! What did I just say?

134
00:06:07,497 --> 00:06:11,153
Now drop
and give me 50. Now!

135
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:13,460
Know anyone who may
have wanted to harm Natalie?

136
00:06:13,547 --> 00:06:16,506
No, but...we did have
a kid go missing

137
00:06:16,593 --> 00:06:18,029
from the facility
last night.

138
00:06:18,116 --> 00:06:20,118
Trent didn't have
anything to do with this.

139
00:06:20,205 --> 00:06:22,860
- His name was Trent?
- Trent Matthews. He's 17.

140
00:06:22,947 --> 00:06:24,775
Was here for drug possession
and assault.

141
00:06:24,862 --> 00:06:26,386
What time did he go missing?

142
00:06:26,473 --> 00:06:28,692
I saw him at dinner,
so after 7:00.

143
00:06:28,779 --> 00:06:31,434
Like I said, he didn't
have anything to do with this.

144
00:06:31,521 --> 00:06:33,393
We'll need to see his file.

145
00:06:34,959 --> 00:06:36,091
Keep going.

146
00:06:38,963 --> 00:06:40,748
You wanna let her
out of prison?

147
00:06:40,835 --> 00:06:43,054
Well, I just think
Erica could help us.

148
00:06:43,141 --> 00:06:45,143
She knows details
of the victim's life.

149
00:06:45,230 --> 00:06:47,798
- She may even know the killer.
- She says she does.

150
00:06:47,885 --> 00:06:49,452
That she's telling
the truth about.

151
00:06:49,539 --> 00:06:52,063
- Doesn't mean we need her help.
- I didn't say that.

152
00:06:52,150 --> 00:06:56,154
- I said she could be useful.
- What do you think, Luther?

153
00:06:56,241 --> 00:06:57,721
- I'm intrigued.
- Sir.

154
00:06:57,808 --> 00:06:59,201
I think..

155
00:06:59,288 --> 00:07:00,724
...it's just the kinda
innovative thinking

156
00:07:00,811 --> 00:07:02,465
the CBI needs more of.

157
00:07:02,552 --> 00:07:06,034
Using a convict to catch
a killer...it's synergy.

158
00:07:06,121 --> 00:07:07,470
Exactly.

159
00:07:07,557 --> 00:07:09,080
Sir, this isn't even
our jurisdiction.

160
00:07:09,167 --> 00:07:11,431
We couldn't get her
released if we tried.

161
00:07:11,518 --> 00:07:13,171
You're right,
but the warden

162
00:07:13,258 --> 00:07:15,478
at Golden Valley State Prison
has already approved it.

163
00:07:15,565 --> 00:07:17,219
Ms. Flynn's guaranteed
a furlough through

164
00:07:17,306 --> 00:07:19,787
the rehabilitation program
that the governor instituted.

165
00:07:19,874 --> 00:07:21,310
[Luther]
'Apparently,
she's a model inmate.'

166
00:07:21,397 --> 00:07:22,920
She's a convicted murderer.

167
00:07:23,007 --> 00:07:25,575
Convicted manslaughterer,
actually.

168
00:07:25,662 --> 00:07:27,751
- Oh, well, in that case..
- So you agree?

169
00:07:27,838 --> 00:07:30,275
No. She's a dangerous killer,
and she's a flight risk.

170
00:07:30,362 --> 00:07:32,495
Which is why I'll be
assigning two agents

171
00:07:32,582 --> 00:07:34,062
to guard her at all times.

172
00:07:34,149 --> 00:07:37,631
See, Lisbon?
What could possibly go wrong?

173
00:07:37,718 --> 00:07:39,284
[Jane]
'Excuse me.'

174
00:07:39,371 --> 00:07:40,503
Synergy.

175
00:07:51,558 --> 00:07:53,647
[exhales deeply]

176
00:07:53,734 --> 00:07:54,865
[cell phone ringing]

177
00:07:57,346 --> 00:07:59,087
- Hey, Cho.
- Hey.

178
00:07:59,174 --> 00:08:00,784
- What's up?
- You called me.

179
00:08:00,871 --> 00:08:02,133
Oh, yeah.
That's right.

180
00:08:02,220 --> 00:08:04,048
I got some background
on Trent Matthews.

181
00:08:04,135 --> 00:08:05,963
He was attending
Sequoia Valley High School

182
00:08:06,050 --> 00:08:08,400
before he was busted
for possession and assault.

183
00:08:08,488 --> 00:08:10,141
It's not far
from the facility.

184
00:08:10,228 --> 00:08:13,405
- Think he might head back?
- He's alone. Family moved.

185
00:08:13,493 --> 00:08:16,017
He's probably looking for
cash and a place to stay.

186
00:08:16,104 --> 00:08:17,584
Might try old friends
for help.

187
00:08:17,671 --> 00:08:19,977
Alright. Van Pelt
and I will get on it.

188
00:08:20,064 --> 00:08:21,979
You ready?
Class is about to start.

189
00:08:22,066 --> 00:08:23,459
Oh, yeah, yeah. All set.

190
00:08:25,461 --> 00:08:28,290
Welcome, mommies and daddies.

191
00:08:28,377 --> 00:08:29,813
My name is Atoosa

192
00:08:29,900 --> 00:08:32,294
and I will be leading
your class today.

193
00:08:32,381 --> 00:08:34,557
Welcome to the first step

194
00:08:34,644 --> 00:08:38,735
in your amazing journey
of parenthood.

195
00:08:38,822 --> 00:08:42,304
Now before we begin,
I would like each of you

196
00:08:42,391 --> 00:08:44,436
to go around the room

197
00:08:44,524 --> 00:08:47,788
and offer something
about yourselves.

198
00:08:52,314 --> 00:08:54,446
Hi.

199
00:08:54,534 --> 00:08:55,535
[chuckles]
Oh.

200
00:08:55,622 --> 00:08:57,406
Would you like to start?

201
00:08:57,493 --> 00:09:01,541
Sure. Um, hi.
My name is Sarah.

202
00:09:01,628 --> 00:09:03,238
Welcome, Sarah.

203
00:09:03,325 --> 00:09:04,674
[laughs]

204
00:09:04,761 --> 00:09:06,720
Oh, hi. I'm Wayne.

205
00:09:06,807 --> 00:09:08,504
Welcome, Wayne.

206
00:09:08,591 --> 00:09:11,725
Um...okay, I'm 28 weeks.

207
00:09:11,812 --> 00:09:14,292
Uh, this is my first child.
Wait. Our first child?

208
00:09:14,379 --> 00:09:15,729
Oh, yeah.
Definitely our first.

209
00:09:15,816 --> 00:09:17,382
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- Our first child.

210
00:09:17,469 --> 00:09:19,994
Well, although "our"
might be a little misleading.

211
00:09:20,081 --> 00:09:21,561
Not that
this isn't his baby.

212
00:09:21,648 --> 00:09:23,824
I'm not some kinda
floozy or anything

213
00:09:23,911 --> 00:09:26,304
and, gosh, not that anyone
in this room is..

214
00:09:26,391 --> 00:09:29,699
[Sarah]
No, I, that is,
I just meant, um..

215
00:09:29,786 --> 00:09:31,222
She meant
that we're not married.

216
00:09:31,309 --> 00:09:33,007
That was it,
that we're not married.

217
00:09:33,094 --> 00:09:34,312
No. I mean, yes.

218
00:09:34,399 --> 00:09:35,575
[laughs]

219
00:09:40,231 --> 00:09:41,755
According
to the youth facility

220
00:09:41,842 --> 00:09:43,713
Trent Matthews was
busted for possession

221
00:09:43,800 --> 00:09:45,454
at this high school
three months ago.

222
00:09:45,541 --> 00:09:46,673
[bell ringing]

223
00:09:49,197 --> 00:09:51,416
You know, kids used
to call me "Bracey Gracie"

224
00:09:51,503 --> 00:09:53,984
because I wore braces
until I was 17.

225
00:09:54,071 --> 00:09:55,595
- What did people call you?
- Cho.

226
00:10:02,427 --> 00:10:03,603
That's him.

227
00:10:05,169 --> 00:10:07,563
[indistinct shouting]

228
00:10:09,217 --> 00:10:10,522
- Hey, break it up!
- Hey!

229
00:10:10,610 --> 00:10:12,350
Come on!
Get off, man!

230
00:10:12,437 --> 00:10:13,874
[female #1]
'Oh, yeah!'

231
00:10:13,961 --> 00:10:16,050
- 'Hey, get off, man.'
- Trent Matthews?

232
00:10:16,137 --> 00:10:18,269
- 'What?'
- CBI. We need a word.

233
00:10:18,356 --> 00:10:20,402
Screw your word, man.

234
00:10:23,840 --> 00:10:24,972
[sighs]

235
00:10:29,890 --> 00:10:32,153
You needn't look
so glum, Lisbon.

236
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:35,112
If anything happens, you're not
gonna be held responsible.

237
00:10:35,199 --> 00:10:38,463
Because that's
what I'm worried about.

238
00:10:38,550 --> 00:10:40,248
[whispering]
You know
why she's doing this.

239
00:10:40,335 --> 00:10:42,206
To try and escape,
most likely.

240
00:10:42,293 --> 00:10:45,906
Yet you're going through
with it anyway.

241
00:10:45,993 --> 00:10:48,430
Are you doing this
because you need Erica's help

242
00:10:48,517 --> 00:10:50,258
or because you want it?

243
00:10:50,345 --> 00:10:52,521
[male #1]
'Agents, you can come in now.'

244
00:10:55,916 --> 00:10:58,483
'You'll have
to sign for custody.'

245
00:10:58,570 --> 00:10:59,702
Thank you.

246
00:11:03,227 --> 00:11:05,882
- Hello, Patrick.
- Erica.

247
00:11:05,969 --> 00:11:09,799
Inmate Erica Marie Flynn
is now in your custody.

248
00:11:09,886 --> 00:11:12,672
- Take good care of her.
- Thanks.

249
00:11:19,461 --> 00:11:20,636
[bell buzzing]

250
00:11:22,725 --> 00:11:25,206
- Alright. Who is he?
- Who?

251
00:11:25,293 --> 00:11:27,643
Natalie's killer.
Don't be cute.

252
00:11:27,730 --> 00:11:30,602
I don't know his name.
It's all in my symphony files.

253
00:11:30,690 --> 00:11:32,953
- Did I not make that clear?
- No, you didn't.

254
00:11:33,040 --> 00:11:35,695
- Must've slipped her mind.
- Where are the files?

255
00:11:35,782 --> 00:11:38,349
My lawyer's having them
sent to your offices now.

256
00:11:38,436 --> 00:11:41,048
Good. Let's get this
over with. You got her?

257
00:11:41,135 --> 00:11:43,485
We got her.
Ms. Flynn, I'm Agent McClay.

258
00:11:43,572 --> 00:11:44,965
This is Agent Morris.

259
00:11:45,052 --> 00:11:47,358
We'll be supervising you
during your furlough.

260
00:11:47,445 --> 00:11:49,926
A friend owns a car company
and has offered me

261
00:11:50,013 --> 00:11:51,623
transportation while I'm out.

262
00:11:51,711 --> 00:11:52,842
How thoughtful.

263
00:11:55,758 --> 00:11:57,760
Patrick, are you coming?

264
00:12:09,032 --> 00:12:10,164
[door closes]

265
00:12:13,689 --> 00:12:14,821
[door opens]

266
00:12:16,605 --> 00:12:17,737
[door closes]

267
00:12:20,696 --> 00:12:21,915
This should be fun.

268
00:12:22,002 --> 00:12:22,916
[sighs]

269
00:12:32,099 --> 00:12:33,230
Here's your tea.

270
00:12:33,317 --> 00:12:34,754
Thanks so much.

271
00:12:34,841 --> 00:12:37,104
- Oh, Ron?
- Yes, Ms. Flynn.

272
00:12:37,191 --> 00:12:39,323
Would you mind getting me
some lemon for that?

273
00:12:39,410 --> 00:12:40,585
Of course.

274
00:12:44,764 --> 00:12:46,417
Hey, boss.

275
00:12:46,504 --> 00:12:48,724
I checked that trip
Natalie took to Puerto Vallarta.

276
00:12:48,811 --> 00:12:50,987
- It seems she traveled alone.
- She meet anybody there?

277
00:12:51,074 --> 00:12:52,206
'I'm not sure.'

278
00:12:52,293 --> 00:12:53,903
We've can't
locate her camera

279
00:12:53,990 --> 00:12:56,688
but Natalie did upload
travel photos on to a web site

280
00:12:56,776 --> 00:12:58,342
I'm having those
printed out now.

281
00:12:58,429 --> 00:13:00,301
- Okay.
- 'Here you go, Ms. Flynn.'

282
00:13:02,129 --> 00:13:03,783
What is it with this woman?

283
00:13:03,870 --> 00:13:06,046
She can get men to do
whatever she wants

284
00:13:06,133 --> 00:13:09,136
and I can't figure out why.

285
00:13:09,223 --> 00:13:10,790
Really?

286
00:13:10,877 --> 00:13:14,271
I get it.
I mean, if I were a guy.

287
00:13:14,358 --> 00:13:15,533
Wow.

288
00:13:18,493 --> 00:13:20,016
[Kimball]
'Assault's
a serious offense, Trent.'

289
00:13:20,103 --> 00:13:21,365
[chuckles]

290
00:13:21,452 --> 00:13:23,019
Man, that dude was a snitch.

291
00:13:25,282 --> 00:13:27,284
That why you were
smashing his face in?

292
00:13:27,371 --> 00:13:30,810
Hell, yeah. He's the reason
why I got sent to juvie.

293
00:13:30,897 --> 00:13:33,290
You ran away from
the facility to get revenge?

294
00:13:33,377 --> 00:13:35,815
No, man.
I left 'cause I had to.

295
00:13:35,902 --> 00:13:37,642
I wasn't about
to get jacked up.

296
00:13:37,729 --> 00:13:39,862
You had a beef
with another kid?

297
00:13:39,949 --> 00:13:43,518
Just one of my counselors,
big dude named Danny.

298
00:13:43,605 --> 00:13:44,824
Danny Vargas?

299
00:13:44,911 --> 00:13:45,955
Yeah.

300
00:13:46,042 --> 00:13:48,653
What happened?

301
00:13:48,740 --> 00:13:52,483
I mean, well, the night
I took off, he, uh..

302
00:13:52,570 --> 00:13:54,921
he and Natalie
were fighting.

303
00:13:55,008 --> 00:13:57,706
I mean, for real,
you know? Um..

304
00:13:57,793 --> 00:14:02,276
She-she was yelling at him like
crazy, man, all up in his face

305
00:14:02,363 --> 00:14:03,799
but, uh, see, Danny..

306
00:14:03,886 --> 00:14:06,628
uh, he's real hard
with us kids.

307
00:14:06,715 --> 00:14:09,544
He, uh,
I mean, he pushes us..

308
00:14:09,631 --> 00:14:12,721
...smacks us around
when no one's looking.

309
00:14:12,808 --> 00:14:15,985
Except this time
Natalie saw it go down.

310
00:14:16,072 --> 00:14:19,032
She wasn't too happy about it,
you know? I mean, the girl..

311
00:14:19,119 --> 00:14:20,947
The girl started
flippin' out on him.

312
00:14:21,034 --> 00:14:22,687
Did things get physical
between them?

313
00:14:22,774 --> 00:14:25,386
Oh, well, it was about to
until I stepped in.

314
00:14:25,473 --> 00:14:27,997
I mean, y-you can't lay
your hands on a woman.

315
00:14:28,084 --> 00:14:30,304
I don't give
a damn who you are.

316
00:14:30,391 --> 00:14:34,047
But, anyway, I mean,
Danny got mad

317
00:14:34,134 --> 00:14:36,963
real mad
so I took off

318
00:14:37,050 --> 00:14:38,747
before he could
do something about it.

319
00:14:38,834 --> 00:14:41,141
You think Danny would have
hurt you in retaliation?

320
00:14:41,228 --> 00:14:42,882
I know he would have.

321
00:14:42,969 --> 00:14:44,579
The dude has
frickin' issues, man.

322
00:14:44,666 --> 00:14:47,887
He-he should be the one
sitting here, not me.

323
00:14:47,974 --> 00:14:49,540
Listen,
with all bull aside

324
00:14:49,627 --> 00:14:52,587
let me tell you
something, alright?

325
00:14:52,674 --> 00:14:56,330
I would never hurt
Natalie, ever.

326
00:14:56,417 --> 00:14:58,201
'I got no reason to.'

327
00:14:58,288 --> 00:15:01,335
I mean, she-she was
one of the only adults

328
00:15:01,422 --> 00:15:04,425
who ever treated me like
a person, you know?

329
00:15:04,512 --> 00:15:05,817
Yeah, I do.

330
00:15:14,696 --> 00:15:17,090
Hey. You okay?

331
00:15:17,177 --> 00:15:19,440
Oh. Oh, yeah. Yeah.

332
00:15:19,527 --> 00:15:22,443
Uh, no.
That video was..

333
00:15:22,530 --> 00:15:24,575
Oh, God. It was horrible.

334
00:15:24,662 --> 00:15:27,274
'I had no idea that
childbirth could be so..'

335
00:15:27,361 --> 00:15:29,798
- Well, so scary.
- Oh, it wasn't that bad.

336
00:15:29,885 --> 00:15:31,408
Sarah, I'm a homicide detective.

337
00:15:31,495 --> 00:15:33,454
I've seen some pretty graphic
things, but that..

338
00:15:33,541 --> 00:15:36,109
...nothing
prepared me for that.

339
00:15:36,196 --> 00:15:40,330
How do you think I feel?
I have to go through it.

340
00:15:40,417 --> 00:15:42,942
Wayne, you're gonna be
okay with this, right?

341
00:15:43,029 --> 00:15:45,335
Yeah, I think so.

342
00:15:45,422 --> 00:15:47,033
- Oh.
- I-I mean, yes. Y-yes.

343
00:15:47,120 --> 00:15:49,209
Alright. Good. Because I..

344
00:15:49,296 --> 00:15:51,080
I can't do this on my own.

345
00:15:51,167 --> 00:15:52,299
I know.

346
00:15:54,475 --> 00:15:56,738
[Erica on TV]
'What kinda man
you looking for?'

347
00:15:56,825 --> 00:15:58,827
[Natalie on TV]
'Well, someone generous..'

348
00:15:58,914 --> 00:16:00,742
'...and caring.'

349
00:16:00,829 --> 00:16:03,832
Someone who puts the needs
of others before themselves.

350
00:16:03,919 --> 00:16:06,748
'I want a man
I can grow old with.'

351
00:16:06,835 --> 00:16:10,230
A best friend.

352
00:16:10,317 --> 00:16:11,622
Problem?

353
00:16:11,709 --> 00:16:13,537
This is so frustrating.

354
00:16:13,624 --> 00:16:16,976
One of Natalie's
interviews is missing.

355
00:16:17,063 --> 00:16:19,282
How unfortunate.

356
00:16:19,369 --> 00:16:22,372
I know what you're thinking,
I had nothing to do with it.

357
00:16:22,459 --> 00:16:24,635
It's not my problem
if your people misplace things.

358
00:16:24,722 --> 00:16:25,897
"My people?"

359
00:16:25,985 --> 00:16:27,812
Alright.
That's enough. Let's go.

360
00:16:27,899 --> 00:16:29,423
- Where?
- Back to prison.

361
00:16:29,510 --> 00:16:32,208
You shouldn't be out
if you can't actually help--

362
00:16:32,295 --> 00:16:33,818
Well, just hang on
a second.

363
00:16:33,905 --> 00:16:35,429
Just 'cause
there's a video missing

364
00:16:35,516 --> 00:16:38,127
doesn't mean she can't help
find Natalie's lover, right?

365
00:16:38,214 --> 00:16:40,912
Absolutely.
It's all right here.

366
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,349
Natalie lived for her work.

367
00:16:42,436 --> 00:16:44,655
She dedicated her life
to helping others.

368
00:16:44,742 --> 00:16:46,222
Her finding love
without my service

369
00:16:46,309 --> 00:16:47,702
can only mean one thing..

370
00:16:47,789 --> 00:16:50,226
...the man she was seeing
was a co-worker.

371
00:16:50,313 --> 00:16:52,141
I tried that. No luck.

372
00:16:52,228 --> 00:16:55,144
That's 'cause she wasn't working
at the facility when they met.

373
00:16:55,231 --> 00:16:57,103
This was ten months ago,
remember?

374
00:16:57,190 --> 00:17:00,410
You mean when she was working
at the nonprofit, Casa Encantar?

375
00:17:00,497 --> 00:17:02,978
Exactly.

376
00:17:03,065 --> 00:17:04,719
- Shall we?
- We shall.

377
00:17:14,903 --> 00:17:17,732
Welcome to Casa Encantar.
Can I help you?

378
00:17:17,819 --> 00:17:21,823
My fiance and I are looking for
a nonprofit to volunteer for.

379
00:17:21,910 --> 00:17:23,346
- Let me show you around.
- Okay.

380
00:17:23,433 --> 00:17:26,697
We're not usually this busy,
but we're throwing

381
00:17:26,784 --> 00:17:28,743
a fund-raising event
tomorrow night.

382
00:17:28,830 --> 00:17:30,875
It's actually
a release party

383
00:17:30,962 --> 00:17:33,574
for a book that
our CEO has written.

384
00:17:33,661 --> 00:17:35,228
Here he is now.

385
00:17:35,315 --> 00:17:37,621
Hi. I'm Greg Relin. Welcome.

386
00:17:37,708 --> 00:17:39,406
It's wonderful,
what you do here.

387
00:17:39,493 --> 00:17:40,711
Thank you.

388
00:17:40,798 --> 00:17:42,583
Since we started,
we've been lucky enough

389
00:17:42,670 --> 00:17:45,716
to build six schools,
four clinics, two orphanages

390
00:17:45,803 --> 00:17:48,980
throughout Mexico,
all in small rural villages

391
00:17:49,068 --> 00:17:50,982
some without electricity
or running water.

392
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:52,854
- 'Mmm.'
- That's our newest orphanage.

393
00:17:52,941 --> 00:17:55,683
[Greg]
'We hope to have four
more by the year end.'

394
00:17:55,770 --> 00:17:57,685
Ifwe raise enough
support tomorrow night.

395
00:17:57,772 --> 00:17:59,730
So Evan's told you
about our gala?

396
00:17:59,817 --> 00:18:01,515
There'll be plenty
of food and drink

397
00:18:01,602 --> 00:18:02,907
'even some entertainment.'

398
00:18:02,994 --> 00:18:04,518
'You're both
welcome to come.'

399
00:18:04,605 --> 00:18:06,781
See, see what
a difference you can make.

400
00:18:06,868 --> 00:18:08,696
Thank you very much
for the invitation.

401
00:18:08,783 --> 00:18:12,221
Tell me, when did you
last see Natalie Gibecki?

402
00:18:12,308 --> 00:18:14,136
- I'm sorry?
- Don't be.

403
00:18:14,223 --> 00:18:16,225
You said you were
looking to volunteer.

404
00:18:16,312 --> 00:18:19,185
I didn't. She did, she also
said I was her fiance.

405
00:18:19,272 --> 00:18:21,143
- Cheeky.
- And you are who, exactly?

406
00:18:21,230 --> 00:18:23,406
I'm Patrick Jane.
I'm a consultant with the CBI.

407
00:18:23,493 --> 00:18:25,278
I'm investigating
Natalie's murder.

408
00:18:25,365 --> 00:18:27,541
[Jane]
'She was seeing
someone here, yes?'

409
00:18:27,628 --> 00:18:29,064
Not that I know of. Evan?

410
00:18:29,151 --> 00:18:31,327
- No.
- No?

411
00:18:31,414 --> 00:18:35,201
Oh, of course. It's a secret,
so you wouldn't tell me anyway.

412
00:18:35,288 --> 00:18:38,943
Mind if I look around,
talk to some of your employees?

413
00:18:39,030 --> 00:18:40,641
- Mmm...no.
- Thank you very much.

414
00:18:40,728 --> 00:18:42,599
Good luck with the book.

415
00:18:47,648 --> 00:18:49,693
[Patrick]
What about him?

416
00:18:49,780 --> 00:18:52,609
Handsome but dim,
like a golden retriever.

417
00:18:52,696 --> 00:18:54,742
Natalie wouldn't be
interested in someone like that.

418
00:18:54,829 --> 00:18:56,874
Who would she be
interested in?

419
00:18:56,961 --> 00:19:01,575
Someone attractive, witty,
compassionate, 25 to 35

420
00:19:01,662 --> 00:19:04,665
fit, good hair,
and a romantic at heart.

421
00:19:04,752 --> 00:19:06,362
Oh, that's all?

422
00:19:06,449 --> 00:19:09,017
No wonder she enlisted
the help of a professional.

423
00:19:09,104 --> 00:19:11,802
Good ones are out there,
if you know where to look.

424
00:19:11,889 --> 00:19:14,631
Natalie was a college girl.
She read voraciously.

425
00:19:14,718 --> 00:19:17,460
She was inquisitive,
intelligent, and idealistic.

426
00:19:17,547 --> 00:19:20,507
She would need to be
with somebody who was the same.

427
00:19:20,594 --> 00:19:21,769
Him.

428
00:19:23,466 --> 00:19:25,773
You buy me dinner
at my restaurant of choice

429
00:19:25,860 --> 00:19:27,078
if I'm right.

430
00:19:27,166 --> 00:19:29,690
No bet. You're right.

431
00:19:29,777 --> 00:19:31,474
He's the only man
that didn't look.

432
00:19:31,561 --> 00:19:33,041
[Jane]
'I'll spring for dinner'

433
00:19:33,128 --> 00:19:35,783
if you can get him
to confess right now.

434
00:19:35,870 --> 00:19:38,089
Ooh. Bet.

435
00:19:38,177 --> 00:19:39,308
Do your thing.

436
00:19:42,964 --> 00:19:46,315
- Hi.
- Hi.

437
00:19:46,402 --> 00:19:48,404
Uh, you must be..

438
00:19:48,491 --> 00:19:50,711
Uh, Richard.
Can I help you?

439
00:19:50,798 --> 00:19:53,844
I'm sorry. Is this a bad time?
I can see you're upset.

440
00:19:53,931 --> 00:19:56,151
What? No. No, I..

441
00:19:56,238 --> 00:19:57,761
I'm-I'm fine.

442
00:19:57,848 --> 00:20:00,503
Uh, bad time
for, for what?

443
00:20:00,590 --> 00:20:03,593
[whispering]
It's okay.
Natalie told me all about you.

444
00:20:03,680 --> 00:20:05,726
I'm sorry. Natalie?

445
00:20:05,813 --> 00:20:07,945
You were having
an affair with her.

446
00:20:08,032 --> 00:20:09,599
That's ridiculous.

447
00:20:09,686 --> 00:20:11,035
I'm a married man.

448
00:20:11,122 --> 00:20:14,213
Don't worry.
I won't tell anyone.

449
00:20:14,300 --> 00:20:15,997
Natalie was
a dear friend of mine.

450
00:20:16,084 --> 00:20:18,434
Her passing has been
devastating for me.

451
00:20:18,521 --> 00:20:21,785
I can't begin to imagine
how you must feel right now.

452
00:20:21,872 --> 00:20:24,832
There's no greater loss than
the loss of the person you love.

453
00:20:27,356 --> 00:20:30,707
I didn't think
that she told anyone.

454
00:20:30,794 --> 00:20:32,013
This is Richard.

455
00:20:32,100 --> 00:20:33,449
There's this
great place downtown.

456
00:20:33,536 --> 00:20:34,972
Sicilian chef. Mmm.

457
00:20:35,059 --> 00:20:37,845
He does wonders with
fish fresh, simple.

458
00:20:37,932 --> 00:20:39,934
Remarkable.
I'm suddenly hungry.

459
00:20:40,021 --> 00:20:41,544
- Mmm.
- Hi, Richard.

460
00:20:41,631 --> 00:20:44,068
We had an argument,
but it wasn't a big deal.

461
00:20:44,155 --> 00:20:46,984
- You lied. That makes it one.
- Didn't think it was relevant.

462
00:20:47,071 --> 00:20:49,944
Your shift ended at 8:00,
the same time as Natalie's.

463
00:20:50,031 --> 00:20:51,511
Where'd you go after work?

464
00:20:51,598 --> 00:20:54,253
- To dinner with a friend.
- Right afterwards?

465
00:20:54,340 --> 00:20:55,689
Yes, about 8:30.

466
00:20:55,776 --> 00:20:57,299
This friend have a name?

467
00:20:57,386 --> 00:20:59,258
Jim Clark.

468
00:20:59,345 --> 00:21:01,782
You don't think I did
something to her, do you?

469
00:21:01,869 --> 00:21:04,045
This is insane.
I didn't kill Natalie.

470
00:21:04,132 --> 00:21:05,612
What were you two
arguing about?

471
00:21:05,699 --> 00:21:08,136
She disliked the way
I handled one of the kids.

472
00:21:08,223 --> 00:21:09,877
Thought you were
abusing him?

473
00:21:09,964 --> 00:21:11,487
I got in his face

474
00:21:11,574 --> 00:21:13,707
maybe pushed him
a little bit, okay?

475
00:21:13,794 --> 00:21:15,535
That's it. It wasn't abuse.

476
00:21:15,622 --> 00:21:17,928
Natalie came in here all
bright-eyed and bushy-tailed

477
00:21:18,015 --> 00:21:19,974
thinking she was gonna
connect with these kids

478
00:21:20,061 --> 00:21:23,064
and it's a great idea,
but it doesn't work.

479
00:21:23,151 --> 00:21:24,892
Sometimes getting physical
is the only thing

480
00:21:24,979 --> 00:21:27,068
these animals respond to,
you understand?

481
00:21:27,155 --> 00:21:28,635
Yeah, you're right.

482
00:21:28,722 --> 00:21:30,593
Abusing kids
is against the law.

483
00:21:30,680 --> 00:21:32,726
Do you understand?

484
00:21:32,813 --> 00:21:34,031
Yeah.

485
00:21:34,118 --> 00:21:35,294
Good.

486
00:21:44,259 --> 00:21:46,653
[Patrick]
'Okay. Thank you. Bye.'

487
00:21:46,740 --> 00:21:48,394
Richard Eldridge will be
speaking with

488
00:21:48,481 --> 00:21:51,788
one of my colleagues
first thing tomorrow morning.

489
00:21:51,875 --> 00:21:53,790
We make a good team,
don't we?

490
00:21:53,877 --> 00:21:55,226
Y-you said you had
a question.

491
00:21:55,314 --> 00:21:57,141
Oh, yes. That.

492
00:21:57,228 --> 00:21:59,927
Would you hate me
if I told you I was lying?

493
00:22:00,014 --> 00:22:01,711
These days,
I don't get to spend

494
00:22:01,798 --> 00:22:03,452
much time alone
with charming men.

495
00:22:03,539 --> 00:22:06,542
Well, there's a reason for that.
So you don't kill them.

496
00:22:06,629 --> 00:22:07,891
We all have our baggage.

497
00:22:09,937 --> 00:22:12,896
I've been thinking about you
a lot over the past few months.

498
00:22:12,983 --> 00:22:15,029
I often wonder
how things would be

499
00:22:15,116 --> 00:22:16,900
had we met under
different circumstances.

500
00:22:16,987 --> 00:22:20,164
Thinking about what might have
been will drive you crazy.

501
00:22:20,251 --> 00:22:23,037
Much better to think about
what will happen in the future.

502
00:22:23,124 --> 00:22:24,343
Erica.

503
00:22:24,430 --> 00:22:25,648
I like you, Patrick.

504
00:22:27,824 --> 00:22:30,479
I hope my directness doesn't
make you uncomfortable.

505
00:22:30,566 --> 00:22:32,133
I know what you're doing.

506
00:22:32,220 --> 00:22:33,700
What am I doing?

507
00:22:33,787 --> 00:22:37,573
Seducing me to conceal
your true purpose..

508
00:22:37,660 --> 00:22:39,009
...which is to escape.

509
00:22:39,096 --> 00:22:41,360
Am I..

510
00:22:41,447 --> 00:22:43,187
...seducing you?

511
00:22:43,274 --> 00:22:44,363
No.

512
00:22:46,147 --> 00:22:47,757
I'm not trying
to escape, Patrick.

513
00:22:49,585 --> 00:22:51,892
In fact, you don't actually
believe I am.

514
00:22:51,979 --> 00:22:53,328
No?

515
00:22:53,415 --> 00:22:55,548
No.

516
00:22:55,635 --> 00:23:00,944
Those agents outside the door
aren't to keep me from escaping.

517
00:23:01,031 --> 00:23:04,644
They're to keep you
and I apart.

518
00:23:04,731 --> 00:23:08,038
I know you have feelings
for me.

519
00:23:08,125 --> 00:23:10,214
This whole escape nonsense
is just your way

520
00:23:10,301 --> 00:23:11,868
of avoiding those feelings.

521
00:23:11,955 --> 00:23:13,522
No, actually
I'm fairly concerned

522
00:23:13,609 --> 00:23:15,394
you might try to escape.

523
00:23:15,481 --> 00:23:17,961
Then ask yourself this.

524
00:23:18,048 --> 00:23:20,224
If those agents weren't
outside the door right now

525
00:23:20,311 --> 00:23:21,748
what would you do?

526
00:23:25,012 --> 00:23:26,230
What will you do?

527
00:23:31,279 --> 00:23:33,673
[intense music]

528
00:23:51,604 --> 00:23:53,997
[instrumental music]

529
00:24:13,190 --> 00:24:15,541
[indistinct chattering]

530
00:24:27,466 --> 00:24:29,032
[Jane]
'What are these?'

531
00:24:29,119 --> 00:24:30,817
Pictures Natalie Gibecki
took when she was

532
00:24:30,904 --> 00:24:32,601
on vacation
in Puerto Vallarta.

533
00:24:32,688 --> 00:24:36,170
I was checking to see if she met
anyone when she was down there.

534
00:24:36,257 --> 00:24:37,998
- Did she?
- Doesn't look like it.

535
00:24:44,700 --> 00:24:46,441
I guess I was done
with those.

536
00:24:53,056 --> 00:24:57,017
Natalie and I s-started seeing
each other about a year ago.

537
00:24:57,104 --> 00:24:59,846
You were having an affair.

538
00:24:59,933 --> 00:25:02,196
Yes.

539
00:25:02,283 --> 00:25:04,503
But I wasn't just
stringing her along.

540
00:25:04,590 --> 00:25:07,375
I planned to leave my wife,
it's just..

541
00:25:07,462 --> 00:25:10,813
[sighs]
You know, it's complicated.

542
00:25:10,900 --> 00:25:12,511
Uh, complicated?

543
00:25:12,598 --> 00:25:15,035
Because your wife's family
has millions of dollars

544
00:25:15,122 --> 00:25:17,124
and you make minimum wage
at a nonprofit?

545
00:25:19,779 --> 00:25:22,259
'What did Natalie think
about your being married?'

546
00:25:22,346 --> 00:25:26,525
[sighs]
She was patient at first.

547
00:25:26,612 --> 00:25:28,962
She knew that I was unhappy.

548
00:25:29,049 --> 00:25:31,225
Recently, she got tired
of waiting.

549
00:25:31,312 --> 00:25:32,922
So she broke things off.

550
00:25:33,009 --> 00:25:36,535
- When was that?
- Two weeks ago.

551
00:25:36,622 --> 00:25:39,320
We hardly spoke during
the entire time. I called her.

552
00:25:39,407 --> 00:25:41,365
I asked her to see me.
She wouldn't.

553
00:25:41,452 --> 00:25:45,718
She said she needed to get away.
Clear her head.

554
00:25:45,805 --> 00:25:48,459
And is that why she went
to Puerto Vallarta?

555
00:25:48,547 --> 00:25:50,766
Yes.

556
00:25:50,853 --> 00:25:55,031
I just assumed that
that was the end.

557
00:25:55,118 --> 00:25:57,556
Then a few days ago,
she called.

558
00:25:57,643 --> 00:25:59,514
She wanted to see me.

559
00:25:59,601 --> 00:26:02,473
She was going to meet you
the night she was killed?

560
00:26:02,561 --> 00:26:04,563
Yes.

561
00:26:04,650 --> 00:26:08,436
9 o'clock. The same little bar
we always go to.

562
00:26:08,523 --> 00:26:11,178
I waited an hour.

563
00:26:11,265 --> 00:26:14,268
When she didn't show,
I just..

564
00:26:14,355 --> 00:26:16,096
I assumed that
she changed her mind.

565
00:26:19,534 --> 00:26:22,319
I-I know that, that you're just,
you're doing your job

566
00:26:22,406 --> 00:26:24,060
Agent Lisbon.

567
00:26:26,759 --> 00:26:31,459
I wouldneverdo this
to Natalie.

568
00:26:31,546 --> 00:26:33,983
I couldn't.

569
00:26:34,070 --> 00:26:37,160
Natalie was going to meet you
the night she was killed.

570
00:26:37,247 --> 00:26:39,554
A married man she was
romantically involved with

571
00:26:39,641 --> 00:26:42,644
who doesn't have an alibi
for the night of her murder.

572
00:26:42,731 --> 00:26:44,603
You'll forgive me
if I'm a little skeptical.

573
00:26:49,346 --> 00:26:51,000
[Van Pelt]
'What about the boyfriend?'

574
00:26:51,087 --> 00:26:53,612
He was gonna meet Natalie
the night she was killed.

575
00:26:53,699 --> 00:26:55,744
Here's the place's name.
Talk to the bartender.

576
00:26:55,831 --> 00:26:58,181
See if anybody remembers
seeing him.

577
00:26:58,268 --> 00:27:01,184
Where's Erica?
Getting a mani-pedi?

578
00:27:01,271 --> 00:27:03,056
- How do you know?
- Alright.

579
00:27:03,143 --> 00:27:05,232
This is getting ridiculous.
Erica's served her purpose.

580
00:27:05,319 --> 00:27:07,016
Time to bring her
back to prison.

581
00:27:07,103 --> 00:27:09,715
- Oh, we can't do that.
- Why not?

582
00:27:09,802 --> 00:27:10,846
I need her.

583
00:27:25,034 --> 00:27:27,428
[indistinct chattering]

584
00:27:29,386 --> 00:27:31,606
Mr. Jane, Miss Flynn.
How nice to see you.

585
00:27:31,693 --> 00:27:33,521
You are here as guests?

586
00:27:33,608 --> 00:27:35,915
Uh, well, not,
not exactly.

587
00:27:36,002 --> 00:27:37,917
I hope there's not
some problem.

588
00:27:38,004 --> 00:27:39,396
Mr. Relin didn't tell you?

589
00:27:39,483 --> 00:27:41,355
Tell me what?

590
00:27:41,442 --> 00:27:43,052
Erica and I
are performing tonight.

591
00:27:43,139 --> 00:27:45,054
Just a little something
we've been working on.

592
00:27:45,141 --> 00:27:46,403
It's all been arranged.

593
00:27:46,490 --> 00:27:49,232
Um, how fantastic.

594
00:27:49,319 --> 00:27:50,799
Well, let's hope.

595
00:27:56,022 --> 00:27:58,415
[guests applauding]

596
00:27:59,765 --> 00:28:01,375
[Jane]
Thank you.

597
00:28:01,462 --> 00:28:02,724
Good evening,
ladies and gentlemen.

598
00:28:02,811 --> 00:28:05,031
My name is Patrick Jane.

599
00:28:05,118 --> 00:28:07,120
For tonight
and for a very good cause

600
00:28:07,207 --> 00:28:11,428
let's all imagine that
this, uh, tawdry hotel ballroom

601
00:28:11,515 --> 00:28:15,606
is, in fact,
the Casa Encantar.

602
00:28:15,694 --> 00:28:18,479
The enchanted house.

603
00:28:18,566 --> 00:28:21,351
Ladies and gentlemen,
my lovely assistant, Erica.

604
00:28:21,438 --> 00:28:22,831
[guests applauding]

605
00:28:22,918 --> 00:28:25,616
Erica and I
will conjure up spirits

606
00:28:25,704 --> 00:28:27,793
that will awe and amaze you.

607
00:28:27,880 --> 00:28:30,230
And then we will turn
that awed amazement

608
00:28:30,317 --> 00:28:34,800
into cold, hard cash that will
help feed, clothe and educate

609
00:28:34,887 --> 00:28:36,932
'thousands of homeless orphans.'

610
00:28:37,019 --> 00:28:38,107
[guests applauding]

611
00:28:40,327 --> 00:28:42,721
'As you can see,
Erica has..'

612
00:28:42,808 --> 00:28:45,593
...set the stage
with four boxes.

613
00:28:45,680 --> 00:28:47,813
Now in order for this
performance to work

614
00:28:47,900 --> 00:28:50,772
we need four willing volunteers.

615
00:28:50,859 --> 00:28:53,862
Once you're chosen, please make
your way promptly to the stage.

616
00:28:53,949 --> 00:28:56,212
Don't be shy. This shouldn't
hurt one little bit.

617
00:28:56,299 --> 00:28:57,605
[indistinct chattering]

618
00:28:59,868 --> 00:29:01,565
A quick hand
for these brave souls.

619
00:29:01,652 --> 00:29:03,524
[guests applauding]

620
00:29:03,611 --> 00:29:07,484
Thank you, Erica.
Looking fetching in green.

621
00:29:07,571 --> 00:29:11,227
Now, ladies and gentlemen,
please pay close attention.

622
00:29:11,314 --> 00:29:13,099
You're about to witness
something

623
00:29:13,186 --> 00:29:16,232
that I can pretty much guarantee
you've never seen before.

624
00:29:16,319 --> 00:29:17,843
[guests applauding]

625
00:29:21,760 --> 00:29:24,588
You will see something clouded
in the unknown

626
00:29:24,675 --> 00:29:27,678
in a world of clairvoyants
and divination.

627
00:29:27,766 --> 00:29:29,463
A world of spirits.

628
00:29:29,550 --> 00:29:32,727
Now I know some of you don't
believe that spirits exist.

629
00:29:32,814 --> 00:29:37,340
But trust me when I tell you
they are very real.

630
00:29:37,427 --> 00:29:39,865
They're here in this room
right now speaking to me

631
00:29:39,952 --> 00:29:42,128
just as I am speaking to you.

632
00:29:42,215 --> 00:29:45,435
And they're telling me that
one of these individuals here

633
00:29:45,522 --> 00:29:47,786
'is harboring a deep,
dark secret.'

634
00:29:49,962 --> 00:29:52,486
Huh? Don't believe me?

635
00:29:52,573 --> 00:29:56,142
Fantastic. That gives me
the chance to prove it to you.

636
00:29:56,229 --> 00:29:58,753
You, sir.
What's your name?

637
00:30:00,668 --> 00:30:04,150
- Richard.
- Richard, are you here alone?

638
00:30:04,237 --> 00:30:05,325
- Yes.
- Thank you.

639
00:30:05,412 --> 00:30:07,327
Would you step forward?

640
00:30:07,414 --> 00:30:09,285
Inside one of these boxes

641
00:30:09,372 --> 00:30:11,940
is an item that holds
great significance to you.

642
00:30:12,027 --> 00:30:14,900
I don't know which box it's in,
and neither do you.

643
00:30:14,987 --> 00:30:16,902
Am I correct?

644
00:30:16,989 --> 00:30:17,990
- Correct.
- Alright, Richard.

645
00:30:18,077 --> 00:30:19,687
I need you to concentrate now.

646
00:30:19,774 --> 00:30:23,473
Concentrate and clear your mind
of any distractions.

647
00:30:23,560 --> 00:30:27,086
I would like you to choose
two boxes.

648
00:30:27,173 --> 00:30:30,872
Two boxes, either on the left
side or the right side.

649
00:30:30,959 --> 00:30:32,091
Please.

650
00:30:34,093 --> 00:30:35,311
Erica.

651
00:30:38,227 --> 00:30:39,315
'There's two boxes left.'

652
00:30:39,402 --> 00:30:41,187
I'd like you
to choose one, Richard.

653
00:30:49,064 --> 00:30:53,503
Now you made your choice only
with the spirits as your guide?

654
00:30:53,590 --> 00:30:55,027
Yes.

655
00:30:55,114 --> 00:30:57,116
Erica, if you would open
the box, please.

656
00:31:04,166 --> 00:31:06,125
Does this necklace mean
anything to you, Richard?

657
00:31:09,737 --> 00:31:11,173
Yes.

658
00:31:11,260 --> 00:31:13,001
Tell the audience
what it means, Richard.

659
00:31:15,569 --> 00:31:16,875
[crying]

660
00:31:19,007 --> 00:31:22,445
It's the necklace
that I gave to Natalie.

661
00:31:22,532 --> 00:31:24,491
[Jane]
'Why did you give it to her?'

662
00:31:27,886 --> 00:31:32,020
It was a symbol
of my deep and abiding..

663
00:31:32,107 --> 00:31:33,326
...love..

664
00:31:33,413 --> 00:31:34,718
[crying]
...for her.

665
00:31:34,805 --> 00:31:36,459
[Jane]
'It's okay.'

666
00:31:36,546 --> 00:31:38,157
It's okay.

667
00:31:38,244 --> 00:31:39,636
[guests applauding]

668
00:31:39,723 --> 00:31:41,247
'Thank you, Richard.'

669
00:31:41,334 --> 00:31:44,032
If you'll make your way back
to your seat, that's okay.

670
00:31:44,119 --> 00:31:47,862
Wait! The spirits are sending me
another message.

671
00:31:47,949 --> 00:31:50,778
They're telling me that
someone else on this stage

672
00:31:50,865 --> 00:31:52,258
has a secret.

673
00:31:54,086 --> 00:31:55,174
Mr. Relin.

674
00:31:55,261 --> 00:31:57,132
[guests applauding]

675
00:31:57,219 --> 00:31:59,526
A crowd favorite.

676
00:31:59,613 --> 00:32:02,355
You're harboring a deep,
dark secret, aren't you?

677
00:32:02,442 --> 00:32:04,487
I don't think so.

678
00:32:04,574 --> 00:32:06,402
Oh, really?

679
00:32:06,489 --> 00:32:09,884
Well, let's check, shall we?
Step forward, please.

680
00:32:09,971 --> 00:32:11,973
Clear your mind
and choose two boxes.

681
00:32:16,412 --> 00:32:17,631
Erica.

682
00:32:19,938 --> 00:32:21,896
Now you know the drill.
One box.

683
00:32:27,728 --> 00:32:30,165
Thank you.

684
00:32:30,252 --> 00:32:34,126
Now you chose this box
of your own free will, yes?

685
00:32:34,213 --> 00:32:35,301
I guess so.

686
00:32:35,388 --> 00:32:37,303
Erica, please do the honors.

687
00:32:37,390 --> 00:32:38,608
Open the box.

688
00:32:41,481 --> 00:32:45,572
Is this photograph
of any significance to you?

689
00:32:45,659 --> 00:32:47,922
- No.
- Are you certain?

690
00:32:48,009 --> 00:32:50,533
Well, perhaps
if you saw it bigger.

691
00:32:50,620 --> 00:32:52,753
Erica?

692
00:32:52,840 --> 00:32:55,016
Now do you recognize it?

693
00:32:55,103 --> 00:32:58,846
It looks like the site you claim
to have built an orphanage on.

694
00:32:58,933 --> 00:33:01,414
'Only there's no orphanage.'

695
00:33:01,501 --> 00:33:03,633
I don't, I don't know
what you're talking about.

696
00:33:03,720 --> 00:33:05,679
What about now?

697
00:33:05,766 --> 00:33:08,247
'It's a photo taken a week ago.'

698
00:33:08,334 --> 00:33:09,596
[guests murmuring]

699
00:33:09,683 --> 00:33:11,859
'There is no orphanage, Greg.'

700
00:33:11,946 --> 00:33:14,993
Only a doctored photograph
you've been passing off as real.

701
00:33:15,080 --> 00:33:17,865
Everything you've said
you've done is a lie, Greg.

702
00:33:17,952 --> 00:33:20,476
- You don't understand.
- Oh, but I thinktheydo.

703
00:33:20,563 --> 00:33:22,957
[indistinct chattering]

704
00:33:25,046 --> 00:33:27,875
You're under arrest.

705
00:33:27,962 --> 00:33:29,964
Let's go.

706
00:33:30,051 --> 00:33:32,880
Uh, thank you.
You've been a lovely audience.

707
00:33:32,967 --> 00:33:34,969
Thank you and goodnight.

708
00:33:35,056 --> 00:33:37,450
[guests shouting]

709
00:33:42,281 --> 00:33:45,240
[Lisbon]
'You embezzled millions
of dollars meant for charity'

710
00:33:45,327 --> 00:33:48,765
and siphoned the money
into your own pockets.

711
00:33:48,852 --> 00:33:51,072
You had everybody fooled
until Natalie took that

712
00:33:51,159 --> 00:33:52,378
trip to Mexico.

713
00:33:55,729 --> 00:33:57,818
Natalie called me.

714
00:33:57,905 --> 00:34:00,951
Said she needed to speak with me
about something important.

715
00:34:01,039 --> 00:34:04,825
So I met her after work
at the subway station.

716
00:34:04,912 --> 00:34:06,218
I offered her a ride.

717
00:34:10,222 --> 00:34:12,441
She told me she had visited

718
00:34:12,528 --> 00:34:14,661
one of the orphanages
that we built.

719
00:34:14,748 --> 00:34:16,358
And she accused you
of lying.

720
00:34:16,445 --> 00:34:17,533
No.

721
00:34:19,709 --> 00:34:21,102
Not at first.
She trusted me.

722
00:34:24,018 --> 00:34:26,847
She wanted an explanation.

723
00:34:26,934 --> 00:34:29,371
But..

724
00:34:29,458 --> 00:34:31,417
...I didn't have one.
What could I say?

725
00:34:31,504 --> 00:34:32,896
She had the photos.

726
00:34:38,119 --> 00:34:40,252
My whole world was threatened.

727
00:34:40,339 --> 00:34:42,036
Everything I had built
would be gone.

728
00:34:42,123 --> 00:34:44,517
[dramatic music]

729
00:34:56,137 --> 00:34:57,182
[sighing]

730
00:34:58,922 --> 00:35:00,881
Okay, I'm coming, Wayne.

731
00:35:00,968 --> 00:35:02,274
- In here.
- Ah!

732
00:35:02,361 --> 00:35:04,537
What is going on with you?

733
00:35:04,624 --> 00:35:05,799
[whispering]
Take a seat.

734
00:35:07,583 --> 00:35:09,498
[sighing]

735
00:35:13,372 --> 00:35:15,156
- Sarah, I, uh..
- Oh!

736
00:35:15,243 --> 00:35:17,941
There's something
I have to say to you.

737
00:35:18,028 --> 00:35:20,988
So I've been thinking a lot
about us these last few days

738
00:35:21,075 --> 00:35:22,642
and, uh..

739
00:35:22,729 --> 00:35:24,861
- ...our situation.
- Our situation?

740
00:35:24,948 --> 00:35:26,211
Yeah.

741
00:35:26,298 --> 00:35:27,255
- Oh!
- And, uh...

742
00:35:27,342 --> 00:35:28,778
...I want it to change.

743
00:35:28,865 --> 00:35:31,041
Are you breaking up
with me?

744
00:35:31,129 --> 00:35:32,217
The opposite.

745
00:35:37,309 --> 00:35:39,789
Will you marry me?

746
00:35:39,876 --> 00:35:42,314
Ah!

747
00:35:42,401 --> 00:35:44,751
- Oh, no.
- No?

748
00:35:44,838 --> 00:35:46,535
I don't wanna get married
like this.

749
00:35:46,622 --> 00:35:48,320
Like what?

750
00:35:48,407 --> 00:35:50,844
I don't want you to propose me
because I'm pregnant.

751
00:35:50,931 --> 00:35:54,978
It's, it's, it's so not fair
to you or to me.

752
00:35:55,065 --> 00:35:58,156
[sighs]
I don't wanna live
the rest of my life

753
00:35:58,243 --> 00:36:01,420
constantly wondering
whether my husband loves me.

754
00:36:01,507 --> 00:36:03,900
Oh!

755
00:36:03,987 --> 00:36:07,991
Wayne, gosh,
you are...you are a great man.

756
00:36:08,078 --> 00:36:12,605
No, and you are going to be
the most amazing father.

757
00:36:12,692 --> 00:36:15,390
[laughing]
Really.

758
00:36:15,477 --> 00:36:18,176
But, gosh, we are
just not ready for this.

759
00:36:39,501 --> 00:36:40,633
[sighs]

760
00:36:44,637 --> 00:36:46,769
Thank you, Patrick.

761
00:36:46,856 --> 00:36:50,599
You have no idea
how much this meant to me.

762
00:36:50,686 --> 00:36:54,647
You know, you didn't have
to leave the other night.

763
00:36:54,734 --> 00:36:57,476
We can't have
everything we want.

764
00:36:57,563 --> 00:36:58,912
Since when?

765
00:37:01,523 --> 00:37:03,221
If you'll excuse me,
I'm gonna go

766
00:37:03,308 --> 00:37:04,787
freshen up
before the car ride.

767
00:37:04,874 --> 00:37:07,703
Don't bother.
I know about your lawyer.

768
00:37:07,790 --> 00:37:09,444
Lawyer? What lawyer?

769
00:37:12,317 --> 00:37:14,057
'We found him a block away'

770
00:37:14,144 --> 00:37:16,930
with two suitcases, cash
and a forged passport.

771
00:37:18,845 --> 00:37:20,412
[male #1]
'I'm sorry, Erica.'

772
00:37:20,499 --> 00:37:22,327
I love you.

773
00:37:22,414 --> 00:37:23,371
I'll wait for you.

774
00:37:23,458 --> 00:37:24,372
Touching.

775
00:37:27,767 --> 00:37:29,116
So it's over.

776
00:37:29,203 --> 00:37:32,728
[sighing]
You can't blame a girl
for trying.

777
00:37:32,815 --> 00:37:34,426
I'd expect nothing less.

778
00:37:38,430 --> 00:37:42,216
[sighs]
It was nice to see you,
Patrick.

779
00:37:42,303 --> 00:37:43,478
I had a lovely time.

780
00:37:45,785 --> 00:37:46,829
Me, too.

781
00:37:49,876 --> 00:37:51,617
Goodbye.

782
00:37:51,704 --> 00:37:55,490
Well, when you say it like that,
it makes it sound like forever.

783
00:37:55,577 --> 00:37:57,100
Just 15 to 20.

784
00:38:01,801 --> 00:38:04,107
- Just sign here?
- Yes, sir. Bottom of the page.

785
00:38:09,939 --> 00:38:11,245
Time to go, ma'am.

786
00:38:11,332 --> 00:38:12,420
Of course.

787
00:38:15,249 --> 00:38:17,643
[instrumental music]

788
00:38:52,939 --> 00:38:55,637
[Wainright]
'Glad that all worked out.'

789
00:38:55,724 --> 00:38:56,682
Yeah.

790
00:39:03,819 --> 00:39:05,560
Special Agent,
Luther Wainright?

791
00:39:05,647 --> 00:39:07,214
'I'm Officer Hopkins'

792
00:39:07,301 --> 00:39:09,695
from Golden Valley State
Correctional Institution.

793
00:39:09,782 --> 00:39:12,480
We're here to take custody
of Erica Flynn.

794
00:39:12,567 --> 00:39:14,874
I'm sorry. I'm confused.
I just signed custody.

795
00:39:17,224 --> 00:39:18,399
[Hopkins]
'Sir?'

796
00:39:31,673 --> 00:39:33,980
The US Marshals are helping
with the search.

797
00:39:34,067 --> 00:39:37,505
She's been flagged on the flight
lists and all border crossings.

798
00:39:37,592 --> 00:39:39,551
You're wasting your time.

799
00:39:39,638 --> 00:39:40,769
Thanks for your optimism.

800
00:39:45,034 --> 00:39:47,472
I have to ask, Jane.

801
00:39:47,559 --> 00:39:49,865
Did you know
Erica was gonna do this?

802
00:39:49,952 --> 00:39:51,606
Try to escape?

803
00:39:51,693 --> 00:39:55,305
Of course.
I mean, who wouldn't?

804
00:39:55,393 --> 00:39:58,308
You didn't answer my question.

805
00:39:58,396 --> 00:40:00,615
No, I didn't..

806
00:40:00,702 --> 00:40:02,095
...answer your question.

807
00:40:05,054 --> 00:40:07,013
[thundering]

808
00:40:11,321 --> 00:40:13,541
[phone ringing]

809
00:40:16,109 --> 00:40:17,284
[clears throat]

810
00:40:20,461 --> 00:40:22,332
- Hello?
- 'Hello, Patrick.'

811
00:40:22,420 --> 00:40:25,118
[Erica]
'I wanted to thank you
for dinner the other night.'

812
00:40:25,205 --> 00:40:27,903
It was the best date
I've had in years.

813
00:40:27,990 --> 00:40:29,818
It wasn't a date.

814
00:40:29,905 --> 00:40:31,646
If you say so.

815
00:40:31,733 --> 00:40:34,170
- 'Where are you?'
- Someplace warm.

816
00:40:34,257 --> 00:40:36,521
Why? Do you miss me?

817
00:40:36,608 --> 00:40:39,828
[chuckles]
Something like that.

818
00:40:39,915 --> 00:40:42,918
You know, Patrick,
we'd have been good together.

819
00:40:43,005 --> 00:40:44,442
Wouldbe good together.

820
00:40:44,529 --> 00:40:45,878
I will find you.

821
00:40:45,965 --> 00:40:48,315
It's only a matter of time.

822
00:40:48,402 --> 00:40:49,708
Oh, Patrick.

823
00:40:49,795 --> 00:40:51,318
I'm almost looking forward
to it.

824
00:40:59,587 --> 00:41:01,981
[instrumental music]

825
00:41:18,867 --> 00:41:20,521
[theme music]

